<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=hand-axe">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Tools and materials</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hand axe</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">Acheulean</span> · Also known as Handaxe, Biface, Acheulean hand axe</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A hand axe is a prehistoric <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stone-tools">stone tool</a> with two faces, usually of flint or chert, shaped by knapping. It is the longest-used tool in human history, characteristic of the Acheulean and the Middle Palaeolithic and made by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/homo-erectus">Homo erectus</a> and other early humans. Early examples date to about 1.6 million years ago, and the Acheulean industries in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a> appeared around 1.4 million years ago. In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> the oldest hand axes appear after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mindel">Mindel</a> Glaciation. The first published drawing of one, by John Frere, appeared in 1800.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hand-axe.jpg" alt="Hand axe" width="330" height="165" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Didier Descouens · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Biface_Silex_Venerque_MHNT_PRE_.2009.0.194.1_Fond.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>c. 1.4 million years ago</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>Southern Ethiopia</dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>The oldest hand axe, from Konso-Gardula, could be 1.9 million years old, and early examples are dated to 1.6 million years ago in the later Oldowan.</p><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Built on</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/stone-tools">Stone tools<span>3.3 million years ago</span></a></div><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=hand-axe">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
